== P1: critical / BPS-type / equator wall (B = 0) ==
PASS P1a B = 0 (wall geodesic w.r.t. the outer vacuum)  =>  DeltaP = 6 pi G sigma^2 and A = 4 pi G sigma
PASS P1b Coleman-De Luccia critical tension for Minkowski -> AdS (R -> infinity, wall planar & static) is the same relation: |rho_AdS| = 6 pi G sigma^2
PASS P1c the extreme (BPS) wall of N=1 sugra, sigma_ext = 2 chi with |V| = 3 chi^2 (kappa = 1), IS the B = 0 wall: |V| = (3/4) sigma^2 <=> sigma = 2 chi
PASS P1d between two dS vacua a planar static wall (1/R^2 = 0) would need A^2 = -H_in^2, which has no real solution; the sugra extreme-wall formula continued to chi = iH gives a purely imaginary sigma; and V > 0 breaks N=1 susy (the review states supersymmetric minima have V <= 0). So P1 in dS is the geometric threshold B = 0 (wall on the equator of the outer S^4), NOT a BPS statement
PASS P1e along P1: k = e/sigma = sqrt(12 pi x/(2 - x))  (pi to the first power)
PASS P1f along P1: A/H_out = sqrt(x(2-x)),  mean/H_out = sqrt(x(2-x))/2  (pi-free for algebraic x); 1/R = H_out exactly
PASS P1g PROBE-LIMIT THEOREM: at fixed k = e/sigma, beta^2 = 6 pi G sigma^2/DeltaP = 6 pi x/(k^2 (1 - x/2)) -> 0 as x -> 0: every gravitational threshold (beta^2 = O(1): B = 0, A = 0) is unreachable in the probe limit unless k -> 0; P1 cannot fix k there

== P2/P3/P4: net-force-free, full discharge, flux quantisation ==
PASS P2 (i) net-force-free wall: mean = DeltaP/(3 sigma) = 0 <=> x = 2 (or x = 0); then A = -B = 2 pi sigma: the acceleration left over is the wall's own gravity and sigma/H stays free
PASS P3 complete discharge x = 1: H_in = 0 (interior Minkowski), DeltaP = E^2/2; P1 and P3 together fix (x, s) = (1, 1/sqrt(12 pi))
   P1 & P3:  x = 1, s = 0.162868;  mean/H_out = 0.500000, A/H_out = 1.000000, B = 0.00e+00;  target 1/Z = 0.172747;  kappa_eff(mean) = 1.4472 (= sqrt(2 pi/3) = 1.4472), kappa_eff(A) = 2.8944 (= sqrt(8 pi/3) = 2.8944)
PASS P1&P3 point: mean = H_out/2 (Z_eff = 2), A = H_out (Z_eff = 1): a factor Z/2 = sqrt(8 pi/3) = 2.894 and Z = 5.789 above the target 1/Z; not the target
PASS P4a flux quantisation E = n e gives x = 1/n and nothing about k: the target then needs k_n = 3/(2 sqrt 2)/(1 - 1/(2n)); n = 1 gives 3/sqrt2 (the kappa = 1 probe value), n -> infinity gives 3/(2 sqrt2); a Dirac-type condition would carry hbar and relate e to a dual coupling, not to sigma

